target:    tests/docker/lib.sh
gate:      php tests/rehearsal-column-control-test.php
kind:      restore-defect
expect:    the only one that vintage ships
rationale: 4.8.1 ships no admin/index.php: the class and the init_tables() signature live in admin/wp-slimstat-admin.php. Drop that branch and the cell finds no file, includes nothing, creates no tables -- and include_once WARNS rather than fatals, so the run continues and the hydration below creates wp_slim_stats itself, from the dump. The cell then asserts the whole migration against a table the arm never built, and reports PASS. This mutation SURVIVED the first draft of the gate, which looked for the filename anywhere in the file and found it in a comment; the assertion now names the file_exists() candidate. Retargeted from rehearse-upgrade.sh to lib.sh when downgrade-corpus.sh (H4) needed the identical helper: two scripts building the vintage's tables differently would produce a corpus that does not fit the cell it was built for, so there is now exactly one definition and the gate asserts that too.
---
--- a/tests/docker/lib.sh
+++ b/tests/docker/lib.sh
@@ -207,8 +207,7 @@
 run_vintage_installer() { # optional site URL for per-blog lifecycle rehearsal
   wpc ${1:+--url="$1"} eval '
     $dir = WP_PLUGIN_DIR . "/wp-slimstat/";
-    $f = file_exists($dir . "admin/index.php") ? "admin/index.php"
-       : (file_exists($dir . "admin/wp-slimstat-admin.php") ? "admin/wp-slimstat-admin.php" : "");
+    $f = file_exists($dir . "admin/index.php") ? "admin/index.php" : "";
     if ($f === "") { echo "NOFILE"; }
     else {
       include_once($dir . $f);
